# Haiku floppy driver

This driver currently contains the common floppy block-device interface and a PC NEC-765 backend.

## PC media

* 3.5-inch 1.44 MiB: 80 cylinders, 2 heads, 18 sectors/track.
* 5.25-inch 1.2 MiB: 80 cylinders, 2 heads, 15 sectors/track.

The 5.25-inch profile is selected through `disk/floppy/N/1.2m/raw`.

## Amiga

Amiga floppy controllers are not NEC-765 devices. Paula uses a track-oriented DMA/MFM mechanism. The m68k build therefore has a separate backend boundary for Paula register access, track decoding, motor/select control, and write precompensation. The current common driver deliberately returns `B_DEV_NOT_READY` until the platform-specific Paula DMA/track implementation is wired into the Haiku m68k hardware abstraction.

This prevents an x86 implementation from accidentally programming Amiga custom-chip addresses and makes the remaining Amiga work independently testable.
